WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:02.130
- [Instructor] We're told that Pilar

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:05.350
has 85 inches of ribbon.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:09.420
She gives her friend,
Nico, 19 inches of ribbon.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.910
How much ribbon does Pilar have left?

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:15.510
Pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.000
All right, now let's do it together.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.760
So Pilar is starting
with 85 inches of ribbon.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.610
And I could represent that
with what's sometimes known

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.120
as a tape diagram.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.840
I guess you could call it a ribbon diagram

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.180
in this case.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:33.490
So let's say the width of
this rectangle or this tape

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:38.190
or this ribbon represents
the length of Pilar's ribbon.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:43.190
So this is 85 inches of
ribbon right over here.

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:48.120
She gives her friend, Nico,
19 inches of the ribbon.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.150
I'll do that in red.

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:51.410
So gives away 19 inches.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:54.910
So I could think about
giving away 19 inches.

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:57.430
And this is just, I'm
not doing it exactly,

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:59.240
but you get a sense of things.

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:03.810
So 19 inches might be about that much.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:06.850
So that's 19 inches

00:01:06.850 --> 00:01:09.140
that Pilar gives away.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:11.900
So how much ribbon does Pilar have left?

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:16.540
Well, it would be this
section right over here.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:19.740
Now how do we figure out
how much she has left,

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.810
this question mark right over here?

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.470
Well, there's a couple of
ways to think about it.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:26.220
You could say 19 plus the question mark

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.480
is equal to 85.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.010
Let me write that down.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:33.810
19 plus question mark,

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:36.593
plus what we're trying to
figure out, is equal to 85.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:41.030
So the amount she gave away
plus the amount she has left

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:42.550
is equal to 85.

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:45.090
Or you could say if I start with 85

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:47.150
and if I were to take away 19,

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:48.850
well, that's what I have left.

00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:52.500
So you could also say that question mark,

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.210
the amount that she has left,

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:58.967
is equal to 85 minus, minus 19.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:04.670
So what is 85 minus 19?

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:07.010
Well, there is a bunch of
ways that we can compute it.

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:09.750
One way to do it is I could rewrite 85

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:13.330
as 80 plus 5,

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.470
separate essentially the tens
place from the ones place.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.540
We have 8 tens, which
is the same thing as 80

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.660
and then 5 ones.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.480
And then rewrite 19 as 10 and 9.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.260
So if I'm subtracting 19,

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:30.260
I'm really subtracting
10 and subtracting 9.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:33.200
Now why is that useful?

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.010
Well, it's pretty
straightforward to say that

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:40.720
all right, 80 minus 10 is
going to be equal to 70.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.370
Eight 10s minus one ten is
going to be equal to seven 10s.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:47.570
And so I could rewrite this as 70

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:51.663
plus five minus nine.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:55.810
Now, if I just try to figure
out what five minus nine is,

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:57.950
we get into a little bit of
trouble, because nine is bigger

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:02.220
than five, but what if we were
to rewrite nine in two parts?

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.010
If we were to say look,
nine is the same thing

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.740
as four plus five, so
if I'm subtracting nine,

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:09.283
that's the same thing as subtracting five

00:03:09.283 --> 00:03:12.420
and then subtracting four.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.760
And this makes it a little bit easier,

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.360
because we know that
five minus five is zero,

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:23.360
and so we can rewrite this as 70 minus 4.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.940
Now what's going to be?

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:29.730
Well we know that 10 minus
four is equal to six,

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:33.793
so 70 minus four is
going to be equal to 66.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.320
And we're all done.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:41.533
That's how much ribbon, she
has 66 inches of ribbon left.

